course: dictionary
lesson: 13063
title: Feigned: pretending on the outside
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Feigned means pretended. Someone who feigns a feeling shows it on the outside but does not really feel it inside. «She gave a feigned yawn, but she was wide awake and listening.» The yawn was for show. She was not really tired.
explain: Feigned is the past form of the verb feign, so it can be a verb: «He feigned sleep.» It can also be an adjective that comes before a noun, like «feigned interest» or «feigned illness». Writers use it to warn you that a feeling or action is fake.
explain: How can you spot a feigned feeling? Check whether the words and actions match. If a character says «I am so interested!» but keeps yawning and checking the clock, the author is showing you that the interest is not real. Ask yourself: does the action match the feeling?
fact: Feign means to pretend, or to show a feeling or illness that is not really there.
fact: «Feigned» means pretended: shown on the outside but not truly felt.
fact: «Feigned surprise» means a surprised face or voice with no real surprise underneath.
fact: Feigned is the past form of feign, as in «He feigned a cough» (he pretended to cough).
fact: A good check is to swap in the word pretended and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «When the teacher asked who broke the vase, Tom gave a feigned look of shock.» What does feigned mean here? | Very real and deep | Loud and angry | Lost or hidden | *Pretended, not really felt
exercise: Which word means the same as feigned? | Hidden | *Pretended | Quick | Cheerful
exercise: Mia said she had a stomachache so she could skip the test. Her stomachache was feigned. What does this mean? | *She pretended to be ill | She was very hungry | She was really ill | She felt better after lunch
test: «His feigned interest in the story fooled nobody; he kept checking his watch.» What does feigned interest mean? | Anger about the story | Real and deep interest | Interest in watches | *Pretended interest, not real
test: Which sentence shows feigned calm? | *The man smiled and said, "Everything is fine," but his hands were shaking. | The man ran to the shop for milk. | The man shouted and threw his hat across the room. | The man cried because he was happy.
exam: Which sentence uses feigned correctly? | The sky looked feigned and blue. | The lake was feigned and very cold. | Feigned the apple was red and sweet. | *He feigned sleep so his sister would stop talking to him.
